 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "s0",
   "title": "Projectile",
   "text": "A **projectile** is thrown into the air and moves under **gravity only**; its path is the **trajectory**. Air resistance is neglected.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "title": "Independent motions",
   "text": "The horizontal and vertical motions are **independent** (a dropped ball and a ball thrown sideways land together). Treat the two components separately.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "title": "Horizontal and vertical",
   "text": "**Horizontal:** \\( a_x = 0 \\), so \\( v_x = v_i\\cos\\theta \\) is constant. **Vertical:** \\( a_y = -g \\), so \\( v_y = v_i\\sin\\theta - gt \\).",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "title": "Results",
   "text": "\\( H = \\dfrac{v_i^2\\sin^2\\theta}{2g} \\), \\( T = \\dfrac{2v_i\\sin\\theta}{g} \\), \\( R = \\dfrac{v_i^2\\sin2\\theta}{g} \\), with \\( R_{max} = v_i^2/g \\) at 45°. The path is a symmetric **parabola**.",
   "actions": []
  }
 ],
 "formulas": [
  {
   "title": "Projectile motion",
   "tex": "x = (v_i\\cos\\theta)t,\\qquad y = (v_i\\sin\\theta)t - \\tfrac12 gt^2",
   "text": "Independent horizontal and vertical motions."
  }
 ],
 "challenges": [
  {
   "id": "c1",
